\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Yes, God is good- in earth and sky,
\par From ocean depths and spreading wood,
\par Ten thousand voices seem to cry:
\par God made us all, and God is good.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The sun that keeps his trackless way,
\par And downward pours his golden flood,
\par Night's sparkling hosts, all seem to say
\par In accents clear, that God is good.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The merry birds prolong the strain,
\par Their song with every spring renewed;
\par And balmy air, and falling rain,
\par Each softly whispers: God is good.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I hear it in the rushing breeze;
\par The hills that have for ages stood,
\par The echoing sky and roaring seas,
\par All swell the chorus: God is good.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Yes, God is good, all nature says,
\par By God's own hand with speech endued;
\par And man, in louder notes of praise,
\par Should sing for joy that God is good.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. For all Thy gifts we bless Thee, Lord,
\par But chiefly for our heavenly food;
\par Thy pardoning grace, Thy quickening word,
\par These prompt our song, that God is good.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

